# Pin LF for everything text, because this package is authored on Windows and
# mirrored to a public repo by a Linux runner. Without it the two writers
# disagree about line endings and a sync rewrites every file it did not change
# -- a diff of the whole tree that hides the one line that actually moved.
#
# It lives HERE, in the package, and not in the mirror. sync-awtoll.yml clears
# the mirror with `ls -A | grep -vE '^\.(git|github|gitignore)$'`, which
# preserves .gitignore and does NOT preserve .gitattributes -- so a copy that
# exists only in the mirror is deleted by the first sync and silently never
# comes back. Measured 2026-08-23: that is exactly what the first version of
# this file did. Anything the mirror needs must be shipped by the package.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Keep the generated Pages assets byte-stable across both writers too.
docs/** text eol=lf
